{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJNfU5bJoVWw79rdQa7y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sitting 007 is filed as `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=21`. I approved 19 of the 21 rows and returned LLR-355 and TC-389. The verdict is at `docs/reviews/wi-961/007-ADJUDICATE-f6061c0.md`, committed once as 932d2f055 with `WI: WI-961` and `Loop-Session: 20261021T045653Z-213020` in one trailer block.\n\n**The return (LLR-355 and TC-389).** The command prints one line per invocation (recorded, unchanged, open and so on), and it's unclear what each line must say to identify which session or sub-agent it's about.\n- **LLR-355** says the outcomes carry \"the defined identifying details\" but never says where they're defined. The definition lives in IF-306 (role, agent type, agent id), which the row doesn't cite. So the row alone doesn't tell a builder what to emit.\n- **TC-389**'s Expected claims \"Recorded, unchanged, and open outcomes identify each invocation\", but none of its tests check that. They only count those lines or match a message id. Only refused and parent-unresolved lines have their identifying details asserted.\n\nThe verdict's \"Returns answered in the lane\" section drafts the fix as an in-lane rework: state the details in LLR-355 or cite IF-306, add a test that asserts them on recorded, unchanged and open lines, and re-sit both rows. I used that heading rather than `## Dispositions`, as in the WI-960 and WI-969 sittings, so intake doesn't mint a new row for work the lane answers itself.\n\n**Why the other 19 are ready:**\n- **Perspective record and checks:** the perspective record passes `hats.py record ... --check --strict`; PERFORMANCE produced SR-244 and every other applicable hat has a no-finding. `trace.py --strict` and `check_trajectory.py --strict` both exit 0.\n- **Spec's open questions:** the lane's decision D-002 records probes that settle the three facts the spec left unverified (resume, sub-agent coverage, depth).\n- **Rows match the code:** I checked the LLR text against `usage_ingest.py` and the transcript reader in `session_adapters.py`.\n- **Recent fixes:** commit f6061c0 closed three of the coverage gaps the arms map found (TC-391, TC-389's log naming, LLR-353's precedence).\n- **The one remaining gap:** SR-244's no-gate-authority clause still has no LLR. TC-393 verifies it directly, and I judged that an honest state.\n\nI also scanned this lane's, trunk's and the primary spool's session logs and found none with an unterminated header. So LLR-351's rule, that any unreadable log refuses the main-transcript ingest, blocks nothing on this box today.\n\nThe commit hooks passed. They printed three readability worsenings, none in a gating measure, and again said one declared check did not run, so that check didn't grade this commit. I left the untracked `.requested` marker alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7060,"cache_read_input_tokens":163566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7060},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"92e9aba0-20f0-4d14-ab1d-60bebe43c8fc","timestamp":"2026-10-23T02:24:14.216Z","request_id":"req_011CgJNfTJCvhBdxWLBWSMHN"}
